                <pb facs="0754" n="604" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg604"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 7357/6.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Costa Rican Minister to
                        the Acting Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Costa Rica</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August 14,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous conversations I have
                    had the honor to have with Hon. Mr. Bacon, Acting Secretary of State, and with
                    yourself touching present conditions in Central America, I have the honor, by
                    direction of my Government, to inform you that the Government of Costa Rica has
                    recognized the provisional government of the Republic of Honduras presided over
                    by Mr. Dávila.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Calvo.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
